WEBVTT

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:17.809
NO HIGH HEIGUS CONCENTRATION
DETECTED

00:00:36.912 --> 00:00:37.746
<i>Tanikaze!</i>

00:00:37.913 --> 00:00:39.831
<i>The ena is infiltrating your interior!</i>

00:00:42.251 --> 00:00:43.627
Damn it!

00:00:43.794 --> 00:00:45.045
EMERGENCY CHEST MISSILE
STANDBY

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:46.380
FIRE LEFT CHEST MISSILE

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:47.673
READY TO FIRE

00:01:02.646 --> 00:01:03.522
What?

00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:04.648
HIGH CONCENTRATION OF
HEIGUS PARTICLES DETECTED

00:01:21.123 --> 00:01:25.627
<i>Go forth and conquer!
<i>Let there be light!</i></i>

00:01:29.548 --> 00:01:34.845
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:01:35.637 --> 00:01:41.601
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:45.772
KNIGHTS OF SIDONIA

00:01:52.195 --> 00:01:55.699
<i>Our only haven is this fortress</i>

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.785
<i>Wandering among the stars</i>

00:01:58.869 --> 00:02:02.039
<i>Where we tremble with impatience</i>

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.458
<i>Between life and death</i>

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:10.213
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:15.052
<i>Knights Knights Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:02:17.262 --> 00:02:23.185
<i>Those of us who have been led
<i>To gather here</i></i>

00:02:23.935 --> 00:02:29.900
<i>Carry within ourselves the will to fight</i>

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:33.528
<i>Our lives shine their brightest</i>

00:02:33.612 --> 00:02:36.031
<i>In the defense of love</i>

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:39.993
<i>We boldly enter the fray</i>

00:02:40.077 --> 00:02:44.498
<i>The Knights of Sidonia</i>

00:02:52.047 --> 00:02:54.549
BATTLE

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.399
What are you doing?
Destroy the core already!

00:03:22.828 --> 00:03:25.580
The ena has infiltrated
Unit Tanikaze's cockpit.

00:03:25.747 --> 00:03:29.167
The Crimson Hawk Moth's ena
has taken the form

00:03:29.418 --> 00:03:31.002
of Shizuka Hoshijiro.

00:03:31.169 --> 00:03:33.171
WARNING

00:03:33.839 --> 00:03:37.718
This... is not good.

00:03:46.518 --> 00:03:48.145
Tanikaze...

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.772
<i>Nagate, can you hear me?</i>

00:03:51.106 --> 00:03:53.191
<i>You can cut off the ena</i>

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.569
<i>if you close the neck sector
<i>sealing walls!</i></i>

00:03:57.154 --> 00:03:58.321
Izana!

00:03:58.739 --> 00:04:00.741
<i>We have to lose the head!</i>

00:04:01.158 --> 00:04:02.743
<i>Nagate!</i>

00:04:17.591 --> 00:04:19.593
Nagate's pulse is increasing!

00:04:21.136 --> 00:04:23.513
-We've lost power!
-What?

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:31.897
Stop pretending...

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:35.400
to be Hoshijiro...

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:36.610
you damn gauna!

00:04:44.785 --> 00:04:45.660
Are you close?!

00:04:45.911 --> 00:04:48.371
I can almost reach!

00:04:53.877 --> 00:04:56.171
I can't... I can't, Shinatose!

00:04:56.379 --> 00:04:57.964
I'm almost there!

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.466
Just a little more!

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:05.680
Got it!

00:05:06.348 --> 00:05:08.391
SWITCHED TO BACKUP POWER

00:05:09.518 --> 00:05:11.394
EMERGENCY HEAD SEPARATION
NECK SEALING WALLS - CLOSING

00:05:24.241 --> 00:05:25.659
No.

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:46.680
Disintegration confirmed!

00:05:46.972 --> 00:05:49.891
Unit Tanikaze has destroyed
the Crimson Hawk Moth!

00:05:57.983 --> 00:05:58.900
Tsumugi!

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:01.403
TSUMUGI - UNCONSCIOUS
REBOOTING VISUAL SYSTEM

00:06:01.486 --> 00:06:03.196
COMMUNICATION LOST
COMMANDO SQUAD 1

00:06:17.252 --> 00:06:20.046
Unit Tanikaze has secured Hybrid Tsumugi!

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:24.926
SURVIVORS SECURED
WARNING

00:06:25.719 --> 00:06:28.388
Several gauna detected near Unit Tanikaze!

00:06:28.597 --> 00:06:32.017
Closing in from all directions!
They will make contact in a few minutes!

00:06:33.518 --> 00:06:35.020
Tanikaze...

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:36.313
Hold on!

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:50.243
We can't take on this many.

00:06:50.785 --> 00:06:51.828
No, we can't.

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:05.675
Tanikaze...

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:07.469
Tsumugi...

00:07:21.399 --> 00:07:22.525
Come on!

00:07:35.288 --> 00:07:36.873
<i>Tanikaze, you all right?</i>

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.541
Samari!

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:08.613
The Hayakaze strike team
has entered Planet Nine's orbit.

00:08:08.863 --> 00:08:12.409
Strike team, destroy all gauna
approaching Tanikaze and Tsumugi

00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:13.743
until backup arrives!

00:08:13.994 --> 00:08:15.161
<i>Copy that!</i>

00:08:32.971 --> 00:08:35.306
Don't let them near Tanikaze and Tsumugi!

00:08:36.933 --> 00:08:38.893
Damn it, how many are there?!

00:08:39.144 --> 00:08:40.478
They just keep coming.

00:08:40.645 --> 00:08:43.690
Quit your bitching!
We're not letting them through!

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:03.209
GAUNA CORE-PIERCING ROUNDS
WARNING

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:05.879
We got their attention! Here they come!

00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:07.047
<i>Get ready!</i>

00:09:07.338 --> 00:09:11.051
<i>Our mission is to protect
<i>Tanikaze and Tsumugi!</i></i>

00:09:11.259 --> 00:09:13.511
<i>I know that.</i>

00:09:17.015 --> 00:09:18.099
Chief Sasaki,

00:09:18.391 --> 00:09:21.227
how many Hayakazes can we deploy?

00:09:21.311 --> 00:09:23.813
<i>You want to deploy more Hayakazes?</i>

00:09:23.897 --> 00:09:26.941
<i>We only have one launch gate.</i>

00:09:27.025 --> 00:09:29.444
<i>It'll take time to get a large fleet out.</i>

00:09:29.694 --> 00:09:34.115
No, deploy them individually
as soon as they're ready.

00:09:35.533 --> 00:09:38.495
Captain! I suggest we launch
a search-and-destroy operation

00:09:38.578 --> 00:09:39.579
using the Hayakazes.

00:09:40.455 --> 00:09:41.581
What do you mean?

00:09:41.998 --> 00:09:43.625
We use Tanikaze and Tsumugi as bait

00:09:43.708 --> 00:09:46.586
to gather all of the gauna together
in one place on the planet,

00:09:46.669 --> 00:09:49.506
and take Planet Nine
without losing a single unit.

00:09:50.131 --> 00:09:52.675
<i>Use them as bait?!</i>

00:09:53.009 --> 00:09:56.679
Yes, to gather all of the gauna
on Planet Nine in one area.

00:09:58.431 --> 00:10:00.725
That is the only way
we can eliminate them all.

00:10:00.934 --> 00:10:03.269
This is a search-and-destroy operation.

00:10:05.605 --> 00:10:07.774
<i>Without losing a single unit?</i>

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:10.026
Very well.

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:13.238
-Do it.
-Yes, ma'am.

00:10:16.324 --> 00:10:19.911
This will be all for nothing
if we lose our bait.

00:10:19.994 --> 00:10:21.663
Protect them at all costs.

00:10:25.291 --> 00:10:27.085
We'll protect them!

00:10:36.845 --> 00:10:39.264
You goddamn gauna!

00:10:58.032 --> 00:10:58.992
HAYAKAZE STRIKE TEAM SNIPER POSITION

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.418
Damn it!

00:11:09.627 --> 00:11:11.045
Tsuruuchi!

00:11:15.133 --> 00:11:16.676
Stay alert, Tsuruuchi!

00:11:16.926 --> 00:11:18.636
Seii...

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:22.724
Why do you always get to save the day?

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:25.977
You finally made it.

00:11:26.394 --> 00:11:28.229
The secondary team has arrived!

00:11:28.479 --> 00:11:31.065
The third and fourth teams
will be there shortly!

00:11:32.525 --> 00:11:35.653
All units, get into attack formation
upon arrival!

00:11:35.737 --> 00:11:37.155
Mobilize now!

00:11:38.448 --> 00:11:40.575
<i>Break through</i>

00:11:41.993 --> 00:11:44.120
<i>When the time comes</i>

00:11:45.038 --> 00:11:47.165
<i>For your survival</i>

00:11:48.207 --> 00:11:50.335
<i>Set yourself free</i>

00:11:52.629 --> 00:11:56.674
The Hayakazes have delivered all gauna
extermination teams into planetary orbit!

00:11:59.135 --> 00:12:00.094
Good!

00:12:00.386 --> 00:12:02.013
All units, attack!

00:12:02.513 --> 00:12:03.681
Exterminate them!

00:12:03.848 --> 00:12:05.433
Don't let a single one escape!

00:12:05.642 --> 00:12:07.018
<i>Copy that!</i>

00:12:07.185 --> 00:12:09.938
<i>Break through
<i>Knights of Sidonia</i></i>

00:12:10.271 --> 00:12:12.565
<i>When the time comes
<i>Knights of Sidonia</i></i>

00:12:12.732 --> 00:12:16.903
All team leaders, confirm your assigned
areas and make sure there is no overlap!

00:12:20.657 --> 00:12:22.617
One hundred enemy cores remaining.

00:12:22.825 --> 00:12:24.577
En, one went your way!

00:12:24.786 --> 00:12:26.996
Hold still already!

00:12:27.413 --> 00:12:28.873
Ninety...

00:12:29.707 --> 00:12:31.209
eighty...

00:12:31.668 --> 00:12:32.502
seventy...

00:12:33.836 --> 00:12:35.380
sixty...

00:12:35.755 --> 00:12:36.589
fifty...

00:12:37.966 --> 00:12:39.384
forty...

00:12:39.509 --> 00:12:40.343
thirty...

00:12:41.344 --> 00:12:42.428
Just a little more!

00:12:42.762 --> 00:12:43.596
We can do this!

00:12:52.355 --> 00:12:55.650
<i>Disintegration confirmed
<i>for the last gauna!</i></i>

00:12:55.817 --> 00:12:59.070
We defeated all of those gauna.

00:13:08.079 --> 00:13:09.872
We won.

00:13:10.081 --> 00:13:12.500
We defeated all of those gauna.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:16.629
Yes. Something I wouldn't have believed
we could do not long ago.

00:13:18.589 --> 00:13:21.300
We have control of Planet Nine.

00:13:25.263 --> 00:13:26.305
We did it...

00:13:27.056 --> 00:13:31.060
It was a good plan,
Probationary Subcommander Midorikawa.

00:13:33.104 --> 00:13:33.938
Thank you.

00:13:37.275 --> 00:13:40.194
We're safe now, Tsumugi.

00:13:42.613 --> 00:13:44.866
What about Izana?

00:13:45.658 --> 00:13:47.702
I'm right here, Tsumugi!

00:13:50.371 --> 00:13:53.708
<i>You're okay...</i>

00:13:53.791 --> 00:13:55.710
<i>Thank goodness.</i>

00:13:56.419 --> 00:13:57.670
Yeah!

00:13:57.754 --> 00:13:59.422
It's all thanks to you, Tsumugi!

00:13:59.672 --> 00:14:01.507
Thank you for saving us!

00:14:01.674 --> 00:14:03.676
GAUNA: REMAINING CORES 0: ERADICATED

00:14:04.218 --> 00:14:06.554
LIVE UNIT TANIKAZE COCKPIT

00:14:08.723 --> 00:14:12.518
Are you saying they have to return
with that thing in there?!

00:14:12.769 --> 00:14:16.189
<i>All the spare helmets and suits
<i>were damaged as well.</i></i>

00:14:16.272 --> 00:14:19.233
<i>There's no way to remove the ena</i>

00:14:19.317 --> 00:14:21.402
<i>while ensuring the pilot's safety.</i>

00:14:21.736 --> 00:14:23.863
<i>There have been no cases
<i>of an ena attacking a human</i></i>

00:14:23.946 --> 00:14:27.408
<i>after being separated from its core.</i>

00:14:27.492 --> 00:14:30.203
<i>It appears that this ena poses no threat.</i>

00:14:30.536 --> 00:14:34.207
<i>Tanikaze, can you fly here
<i>while carrying Tsumugi?</i></i>

00:14:34.791 --> 00:14:36.125
I can try.

00:14:48.221 --> 00:14:50.139
This is not appropriate!

00:14:53.601 --> 00:14:56.062
-Ready?
-Yes.

00:15:05.905 --> 00:15:09.450
Am I too heavy?

00:15:09.534 --> 00:15:11.494
Not at all, Tsumugi.

00:15:24.549 --> 00:15:30.930
<i>I'm more worried what Tanikaze might do
<i>to the ena, if you know what I mean.</i></i>

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:32.849
<i>Right, Samari?</i>

00:15:33.141 --> 00:15:34.434
Whatever...

00:15:35.143 --> 00:15:37.186
All units, back to Sidonia!

00:16:03.796 --> 00:16:06.841
CONTENTS: ENA
TOA HEAVY INDUSTRIES

00:16:11.596 --> 00:16:13.431
Hoshijiro.

00:16:13.598 --> 00:16:19.479
SITES OF SIDONIA
HAYAKAZE NAVAL DOCK

00:16:23.357 --> 00:16:26.360
We've successfully entered
orbit around Planet Nine!

00:16:26.861 --> 00:16:29.906
-What's the status of the gauna cluster?
-No change!

00:16:31.699 --> 00:16:33.743
We can breathe easy, then.

00:16:34.619 --> 00:16:38.623
But there's no turning back now.

00:16:38.789 --> 00:16:40.082
SIDONIA PUBLIC BROADCASTING NEWS
SIDONIA ENTERS PLANET NINE'S ORBIT

00:16:40.208 --> 00:16:44.587
<i>Today, Sidonia successfully
<i>entered Planet Nine's orbit.</i></i>

00:16:44.837 --> 00:16:47.215
<i>Planet Nine is rich with natural resources</i>

00:16:47.340 --> 00:16:50.551
<i>and the outer rings
<i>provide a natural defense.</i></i>

00:16:50.676 --> 00:16:53.679
<i>The Command Division
<i>has made the statement...</i></i>

00:16:53.763 --> 00:16:55.515
There's no turning back now.

00:16:55.598 --> 00:16:57.141
<i>...for the coming war
<i>with the gauna cluster.</i></i>

00:17:05.608 --> 00:17:10.863
Soon, I will finally fulfill the dream
I failed to realize a hundred years ago.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:11.948
My dream.

00:17:12.907 --> 00:17:16.118
To be reborn a god.

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:23.125
Nagate Tanikaze, in recognition of
the valor and bravery you demonstrated

00:17:23.209 --> 00:17:27.547
in our taking of Planet Nine,
we award you with the Medal of Covenant.

00:17:34.512 --> 00:17:35.805
You're a knight now.

00:17:36.806 --> 00:17:39.100
Thank you. Thank you very much.

00:17:53.656 --> 00:17:54.657
Oh, thanks.

00:17:58.744 --> 00:18:01.581
-Hey, Tanikaze, let me see your medal.
-What?

00:18:02.707 --> 00:18:05.668
Ren, leave him alone.

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:07.712
You stay out of it.

00:18:07.962 --> 00:18:10.965
Congratulations, Nagate Tanikaze.

00:18:11.299 --> 00:18:12.842
Kunato...

00:18:13.884 --> 00:18:16.220
I expect great things from you.

00:18:16.512 --> 00:18:18.764
I wanted to express my gratitude as well.

00:18:18.973 --> 00:18:22.893
Thank you for saving Tsumugi.

00:18:26.814 --> 00:18:28.899
-Kunato...
-What is it?

00:18:30.026 --> 00:18:34.614
Hoshijiro... I mean, the ena,
what happened to it?

00:18:35.031 --> 00:18:38.993
It's being kept
as an extremely valuable specimen.

00:18:40.161 --> 00:18:41.829
I see...

00:18:42.496 --> 00:18:44.999
It's always a good idea to have reserves

00:18:45.249 --> 00:18:47.668
of our important assets.

00:18:57.678 --> 00:19:01.140
Awarding him a medal.
A long forgotten tradition...

00:19:01.557 --> 00:19:04.810
that seemed to improve morale
quite impressively.

00:19:09.398 --> 00:19:10.858
Kobayashi!

00:19:14.153 --> 00:19:17.114
Stop using the boy
for your own political gain!

00:19:17.448 --> 00:19:18.407
Who are you?!

00:19:18.699 --> 00:19:20.034
Wait.

00:19:24.955 --> 00:19:27.208
People are emotionally fragile creatures.

00:19:28.959 --> 00:19:31.212
You of all people should know

00:19:31.295 --> 00:19:36.509
the difficulty of sustaining a long war
after a hero has fallen.

00:19:37.426 --> 00:19:38.969
I have lived it.

00:19:40.054 --> 00:19:41.639
So have you.

00:19:57.822 --> 00:19:59.907
Kobayashi...

00:20:03.202 --> 00:20:04.620
I'm home...

00:20:07.748 --> 00:20:08.582
Huh?

00:20:08.833 --> 00:20:10.918
I'm the first one here?

00:20:18.134 --> 00:20:21.762
IT JUST TAKES A SECOND GRAVITY NOODLES
SUPER EFFICIENT WITH ONIONS

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:29.437
Whoa.

00:20:36.777 --> 00:20:38.487
Tanikaze...

00:20:55.796 --> 00:20:58.799
Ow, hot! That's hot!

00:20:59.258 --> 00:21:01.135
Are you okay?!

00:21:09.268 --> 00:21:11.437
Tsumugi!

00:21:11.645 --> 00:21:13.939
Never do that again!

00:21:16.233 --> 00:21:18.736
What?! What happened?!

00:21:33.667 --> 00:21:36.504
I'll help you apologize.

00:21:36.587 --> 00:21:38.214
And don't worry,

00:21:38.297 --> 00:21:41.342
Nagate could never hate you.

00:21:42.343 --> 00:21:45.137
Do you really think so?

00:21:45.221 --> 00:21:46.055
Yeah.

00:21:47.681 --> 00:21:52.603
I'm sorry I took your uniform
without asking.

00:21:52.686 --> 00:21:54.939
It's fine.

00:21:55.689 --> 00:21:58.901
Come on, don't cry.

00:21:59.902 --> 00:22:03.239
I didn't know you could do that.

00:22:03.322 --> 00:22:07.117
But... why did you choose Hoshijiro?

00:22:08.035 --> 00:22:09.537
Well...

00:22:10.538 --> 00:22:12.081
That's because...

00:22:12.206 --> 00:22:15.209
Tanikaze blames himself
for Hoshijiro's death.

00:22:15.417 --> 00:22:18.504
He's been struggling with the guilt.

00:22:19.255 --> 00:22:21.674
I thought that...

00:22:21.757 --> 00:22:26.053
if I looked like Hoshijiro
and told him that it wasn't his fault...

00:22:26.720 --> 00:22:29.139
he'd be able to feel better.

00:22:32.101 --> 00:22:33.852
I think...

00:22:33.936 --> 00:22:38.524
it was really painful for Tanikaze
to fight the Crimson Hawk Moth.

00:22:40.234 --> 00:22:41.777
Tsumugi...

00:22:44.613 --> 00:22:45.781
Izana?

00:22:46.657 --> 00:22:49.535
<i>It should've been painful for you</i>

00:22:49.618 --> 00:22:52.288
<i>to fight the Crimson Hawk Moth, too.</i>

00:22:58.377 --> 00:23:00.129
Nagate?

00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:08.178
Oh!

00:23:08.304 --> 00:23:09.638
There you two are!

00:23:13.017 --> 00:23:16.604
Tanikaze... I'm...

00:23:16.687 --> 00:23:18.230
I'm...

00:23:18.897 --> 00:23:22.234
I'm sorry I yelled at you before.

00:23:23.152 --> 00:23:28.949
You know, I found a great automated food
stand nearby you should be able to reach.

00:23:29.033 --> 00:23:30.701
Do you two want to check it out?

00:23:32.036 --> 00:23:33.746
Yes!

00:23:35.039 --> 00:23:39.376
Okay. I actually haven't eaten
anything this week yet.

00:23:41.211 --> 00:23:43.589
It's good.

00:23:43.672 --> 00:23:44.965
This is fun.

00:23:59.563 --> 00:24:01.857
You're Pilot Nagate Tanikaze!

00:24:04.151 --> 00:24:06.487
Oh... hello again.

00:24:07.279 --> 00:24:10.407
Oh, I'm really sorry about that.

00:24:17.164 --> 00:24:21.043
Please, make yourself comfortable.
I'll pour you some tea.

00:24:21.210 --> 00:24:23.253
Oh, that's okay.

00:24:23.337 --> 00:24:25.130
I was on my way somewhere.

00:24:25.631 --> 00:24:27.299
Oh, I see.

00:24:28.425 --> 00:24:30.094
Come back any time.

00:24:30.302 --> 00:24:32.805
I'll have a rice ball for you.

00:24:34.807 --> 00:24:37.935
Thank you very much.

00:24:59.456 --> 00:25:03.419
This is the room
you were first admitted to.

00:25:06.714 --> 00:25:10.801
I can't believe that rice thief
turned out to be Pilot Tanikaze.

00:25:10.884 --> 00:25:14.304
Oh, I'm sorry.
I didn't need to bring that up.

00:25:14.513 --> 00:25:19.017
I'm really sorry for all of the trouble
I caused you.

00:25:19.101 --> 00:25:22.062
Oh, you don't need to apologize for that.

00:25:32.364 --> 00:25:34.533
Hey, what are you doing?!

00:25:45.377 --> 00:25:48.255
You're Pilot Tanikaze!

00:25:48.422 --> 00:25:51.216
I have this.

00:25:52.217 --> 00:25:54.428
Access permit.

00:25:56.764 --> 00:25:58.849
I see, you're visiting your old home.

00:26:00.017 --> 00:26:01.310
I know.

00:26:05.230 --> 00:26:06.231
Here.

00:26:08.275 --> 00:26:09.568
Please take this with you.

00:26:09.651 --> 00:26:10.652
RICE

00:26:12.154 --> 00:26:14.865
Thank you... very much.

00:26:19.995 --> 00:26:21.997
NUMBER FOUR FOOD FACTORY
RICE

00:26:35.677 --> 00:26:37.763
To Nagate, do not go beyond this point.
Hiroki

00:26:40.557 --> 00:26:42.226
<i>Grandpa...</i>

00:26:42.559 --> 00:26:44.937
<i>I'm sorry I broke your rule.</i>

00:26:46.522 --> 00:26:48.190
<i>But I'm glad...</i>

00:26:48.273 --> 00:26:50.108
<i>I left here.</i>

00:26:57.199 --> 00:26:59.868
<i>So much has happened.</i>

00:27:00.452 --> 00:27:01.662
<i>I...</i>

00:27:20.013 --> 00:27:24.268
<i>I've grown to love Sidonia even more.</i>

00:27:29.106 --> 00:27:31.441
I'm back, Nagate.

00:27:32.192 --> 00:27:33.777
You're back!

00:27:33.986 --> 00:27:36.530
It's rice!

00:27:40.033 --> 00:27:42.202
Wow.

00:27:43.120 --> 00:27:45.497
Go on, eat up.

00:27:45.581 --> 00:27:48.250
-You can't fight on an empty stomach.
-Okay!

00:27:53.505 --> 00:27:56.174
I'm home, Grandpa.

00:28:03.682 --> 00:28:05.601
VIRTUAL GARDE TRAINING SYSTEM

00:28:14.484 --> 00:28:16.445
Look what they gave me.

00:28:20.532 --> 00:28:23.410
This is the Virtual Garde Training System.

00:28:23.493 --> 00:28:26.455
It's a device that will help train you
to fight the gauna.

00:28:28.165 --> 00:28:30.876
You want to give it a try, Nagate?

00:28:31.877 --> 00:28:33.587
Yeah!

00:28:47.309 --> 00:28:49.019
Nagate...

00:28:49.436 --> 00:28:52.314
you want to become a pilot
that can protect Sidonia, don't you?

00:28:53.398 --> 00:28:57.819
Then no matter how hard or painful things
get, you have to be prepared to fight.

00:28:58.070 --> 00:29:01.240
The gauna won't wait for you
to stop crying.

00:29:06.870 --> 00:29:08.163
Watch me.

00:29:08.914 --> 00:29:11.625
I'll teach you how to fight the gauna.

00:29:23.053 --> 00:29:25.222
DEPLOYMENT ORDER

00:29:27.933 --> 00:29:29.518
Grandpa...

00:29:31.561 --> 00:29:32.980
I have to go.

00:29:34.690 --> 00:29:36.275
On the Tsugumori.

00:29:40.320 --> 00:29:43.532
<i>Gauna 604 has already crossed
<i>the level 1 security border.</i></i>

00:29:43.615 --> 00:29:45.325
<i>It's 180,000 km away.</i>

00:29:45.492 --> 00:29:49.204
<i>Make preparations to deploy
<i>the 12 Western Division units on duty.</i></i>

00:29:49.579 --> 00:29:52.457
<i>Our target is Gauna 604.</i>

00:29:52.833 --> 00:29:55.294
<i>All garde units,
<i>prepare for sequential deployment!</i></i>

00:29:56.336 --> 00:29:59.047
<i>Break through</i>

00:29:59.756 --> 00:30:02.217
<i>When the time comes</i>

00:30:02.801 --> 00:30:05.095
<i>For your survival</i>

00:30:06.221 --> 00:30:08.390
<i>Set yourself free</i>

00:30:10.100 --> 00:30:13.270
<i>The path in space
<i>Disappears in the wind</i></i>

00:30:13.353 --> 00:30:16.523
<i>Peace is several billion light years ahead</i>

00:30:16.606 --> 00:30:19.818
<i>Take the plunge
<i>Do not waiver</i></i>

00:30:19.901 --> 00:30:22.821
<i>Let's go, valiant knight</i>

00:30:24.281 --> 00:30:27.409
<i>Break through
<i>Knights of Sidonia</i></i>

00:30:27.492 --> 00:30:30.454
<i>When the time comes
<i>Knights of Sidonia</i></i>

00:30:30.537 --> 00:30:33.707
<i>For your survival
<i>Knights of Sidonia</i></i>

00:30:33.790 --> 00:30:37.794
<i>Set yourself free
<i>Your path is in your hands</i></i>

00:30:37.878 --> 00:30:41.006
<i>Who do we fight for?</i>

00:30:44.384 --> 00:30:47.554
<i>Who do we die for?</i>

00:30:50.932 --> 00:30:53.310
<i>As soon as you take your oath</i>

00:30:54.102 --> 00:30:57.356
<i>Throw yourself to the cause</i>

00:30:57.439 --> 00:31:00.359
<i>Do not be daunted
<i>By responsibility and exhaustion</i></i>

00:31:00.442 --> 00:31:03.862
<i>Face your destiny</i>

00:31:17.042 --> 00:31:20.212
<i>Do not fear your own demise</i>

00:31:20.295 --> 00:31:23.423
<i>The heavens are only
<i>The edge of the limits</i></i>

00:31:23.507 --> 00:31:26.718
<i>Many were lost in the countless battles</i>

00:31:26.802 --> 00:31:29.554
<i>Keep the fallen in your hearts</i>

00:31:30.972 --> 00:31:34.267
<i>Break through
<i>Knights of Sidonia</i></i>

00:31:34.351 --> 00:31:37.354
<i>When the time comes
<i>Knights of Sidonia</i></i>

00:31:37.437 --> 00:31:41.108
<i>For your survival
<i>Knights of Sidonia</i></i>

00:31:41.191 --> 00:31:44.694
<i>Set yourself free
<i>Your path is in your hands</i></i>

00:31:57.833 --> 00:32:01.002
<i>Who do we fight for?</i>

00:32:04.423 --> 00:32:07.551
<i>Who do we die for?</i>

00:32:12.556 --> 00:32:15.725
<i>As soon as you take your oath</i>

00:32:15.809 --> 00:32:19.020
<i>Throw yourself to the cause</i>

00:32:19.104 --> 00:32:21.857
<i>Do not be daunted
<i>By responsibility and exhaustion</i></i>

00:32:21.940 --> 00:32:25.152
<i>Face your destiny</i>

00:32:25.610 --> 00:32:28.822
<i>Just beyond the destruction</i>

00:32:28.905 --> 00:32:32.075
<i>The stars smile faintly</i>

00:32:32.159 --> 00:32:35.328
<i>Even so, the end of the road is oh so far</i>

00:32:35.412 --> 00:32:37.330
<i>So far</i>

00:32:37.497 --> 00:32:39.708
Tanikaze Squad,
four unit clasp formation!

00:32:39.791 --> 00:32:41.042
Copy that!

00:32:42.419 --> 00:32:45.046
<i>Oh... and...</i>

00:32:46.131 --> 00:32:48.633
<i>I want you to hold on to this for me...</i>

00:32:49.384 --> 00:32:50.844
<i>Grandpa.</i>
